 "notes": [
  "prefill is not a smooth polynomial on this stack: ~75 ms plateau from 512 to 3072 tokens, a step at 4096, then ~13 ms per 1k tokens beyond 8192 (about 77k tokens/s); the quadratic fit has +-20 ms residuals, use the points for a table-driven model",
  "fixed overhead (1-token prompt) 17-24 ms between passes; absolute prefill numbers moved by ~25 ms between the two passes taken 15 min apart on the same worker",
  "decode ITL in the steady window (all streams decoding) grows with KV tokens in use: 3.9 ms at 8x(512+128) to 9.6 ms at 128x(2048+128); whole-stream means are higher because simultaneous starts interleave prefill chunks into early decode steps",
  "one setting per pass showed a one-off multi-second first-token stall (17 s at 128x512 in pass 1, 10 s at 8x2048 in pass 2) while steady ITL was unaffected; likely kernel autotuning on a new shape",
  "GetLoads on the Rust vLLM servicer reports only max_total_num_tokens and max_running_requests (num_used_tokens/token_usage unset), so utilisation here is computed as tokens in use / capacity"
 ]
}
